<title>south africa: Rugby union-Free State stun Waikato with four tries.</title>
<headline>Rugby union-Free State stun Waikato with four tries.</headline>
<byline>Andy Capostagno</byline>
<dateline>BLOEMFONTEIN, South Africa 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Free State kept alive their outside hopes of making the Super 12 semifinals with a 27-13 defeat of New Zealand's Waikato on Saturday.</p>
<p>Free State ran in four tries to one, ensuring maximum five points from the encounter. They responded to early pressure from Waikato, who led 13-10 at halftime, and dominated the final quarter, scoring three tries.</p>
